<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <MSBuildAllProjects>$(MSBuildAllProjects);$(MSBuildThisFileFullPath)</MSBuildAllProjects>
    <HasSharedItems>true</HasSharedItems>
    <SharedGUID>a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a7b-8c9d-bed2c0000001</SharedGUID>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="Configuration">
    <Import_RootNamespace>Birko.Redis</Import_RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- External dependency: StackExchange.Redis — CONSUMER-SUPPLIED, deliberately not declared here.
       Declare it yourself, e.g.

         <PackageReference Include="StackExchange.Redis" Version="2.*" />

       A shared project normally declares its own external dependency (TASK-229), and the Redis family
       is the exception, decided in TASK-234. The rule that produced it: **a family may own a package
       only if every project needing that package belongs to the family.** Five projitems use
       StackExchange.Redis — this one, BackgroundJobs, Caching, MessageQueue and Health — and
       Birko.Health.Redis is not a satellite of this project at all: it talks to the driver directly
       and needs none of the types here. So no project can own the declaration without either coupling
       Health.Redis to five shared projects it does not use (RedisSettings extends RemoteSettings and
       implements ILoadable, so importing this drags Configuration, Data.Core, Data.Stores, Contracts
       and Time), or emitting two PackageReference items wherever both are imported — NU1504, which
       the -warnaserror the build sweep runs turns into an error.

       Contrast Birko.Data.ElasticSearch, which DOES declare NEST: there all six other users are true
       satellites of it, so the family is closed and one declaration covers it.

       Float within the major (`2.*`) rather than pinning. TASK-234 measured why: the float moved this
       family 2.8 -> 2.13 and immediately surfaced two latent breaks — an overload of StringSetAsync
       that no longer bound, and seven tests whose Moq setups named superseded StreamAdd /
       StreamReadGroup signatures. A pin hides that until an advisory forces the bump. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)RedisSettings.cs" />
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)RedisConnectionManager.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
